{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217691-what-happens-when-a-changeling-uses-magic-in-front-of-a-mortal","id":217691,"title":"What happens when a Changeling uses magic in front of a mortal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-03T17:58:10-07:00","id":217691,"title":"What happens when a Changeling uses magic in front of a mortal?","content":"So I get that a changeling suffers clarity loss for using magic in front of mortals, but what exactly do mortals see on their end? Does the mask disguise the magic or do they see it for what it is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:01:15-07:00","id":217853,"title":"","content":"According to the previews of Mage's <i>Fallen World Chronicle</i>, witnessing Supernal Magic is a Breaking Point for mortals; I would imagine that anything similarly overtly-supernatural would impact a mortal mind in similar ways.<br /> <br /> ...but then again, Changelings and many other fae-touched things/beings have Masks that hide them from the mundane world. So perhaps some Contracts conspire to cloak their magical nature from mortals. I don't know if there's an official ruling, but I could argue for it either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T21:12:11-07:00","id":217860,"title":"","content":"A big part of the reason why Changeling's lose Clarity on that is that there's no hiding it from mortals. Any forgetting it is on their own part-they see the sprites dancing in the Fireheart's hands before he sics them on the rapist, they see the shadows bubble off the Whisperwisp's hand before she takes their sight, and the they see the diamond light of the Bright One as it takes their heart.<br /> <br /> In that moment, a human knows that magic is real, that the old stories are true, and that the Good Folk must be appeased. They might forget and rationalize it later on their own, and it may not be as alive for them later as it was then(thus keeping them from crossing over into minor template territory), but that's a choice they make by and large.<br /> <br /> Naturally, breaking down because you had your world shatter in that moment might make it hard to accept and thus properly remember, but peoples is peoples.<br /> <br /> SHORTHAND: Nothing hides Changeling magic except what the Changeling does to hide it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T06:35:20-07:00","id":218083,"title":"","content":"I'm curious about where we're finding that Changelings uses contracts in front of a mortal causes clarity loss?<br /> <br /> And after a lot of research, I found that unless the contract itself has a visual component like Elements Fire, manipulating fire, Contracts HAVE NO visual to them to anyone excepot the Changeling who is using the Contract himself.<br /> <br /> The winter court mentions that an OPTION might be the sight of flakes of snow in the mantle when a Changeling uses a particular contract, but that the only defined visual from Contract use is when the force of the Wyrd shows up, to the contract using changeling ONLY, to collect the terms of the catch metaphysically, or the glamour used to activate the Contract.<br /> <br /> Contract use is virtually invisible almost universally, even between Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T09:09:44-07:00","id":218237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gwiber</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/217691-what-happens-when-a-changeling-uses-magic-in-front-of-a-mortal?p=218083#post218083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious about where we're finding that Changelings uses contracts in front of a mortal causes clarity loss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Corebook p. 92, breaking points for Clarity 6: &quot;Obvious displays of magic in front of witnesses.&quot; As you point out, there are in fact a bunch of Contracts that you can use right in front of a mortal without producing an &quot;obvious display,&quot; but stepping into somebody's bedroom by travelling through a sleeper's dreams with Dream 5, remolding your face with Mirror 2, or a bunch of various other clauses produce an obvious effect that shouldn't be possible without magic, regardless of whether the witness can perceive the Wyrd's influence in realizing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T15:45:54-07:00","id":218575,"title":"","content":"There <i>is</i> a thing on page 124 of Changeling the Lost that showcases that changelings themselves see a visible aspect to all of their contracts, however it is worded in a way indicates that only they see it. Thematically very appropriate, but I've run it with everyone seeing it like that for a long time, so I'm set. You may go and read it yourself, and I think you'll find the reading in favor for just changeling's, but then again you might interpret it differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T15:52:13-07:00","id":218582,"title":"","content":"Mortals can see their magic. It's just that most changeling contracts don't have a visible affect. Some do, of course. But in the first chapter, when explaining hiding, it does explain that changelings can present themselves as sorcerers and magicians.<br /> <br /> So a changeling turning into a cloud of leaves would be seen as a person turning into a cloud of leaves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T15:58:44-07:00","id":218587,"title":"","content":"As an illustration of the thing I'm pointing at, the use of the clause Murkblur in Darkness(I think) can be signified by a fountain of shadows falling from your hands. The understanding from the page I referenced is that mortals won't see that fountain, but the changeling would. It's a confirmation to the changeling that the contract is fulfilled.<br /> <br /> It is loose enough that it can be interpretted that anyone would see that fountain, although it doesn't lean that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T19:24:32-07:00","id":219744,"title":"","content":"My thoughts: <br /> <br /> Changeling magic does not, innately, appear supernaturally to mortals. That is, if a Changeling uses Fleeting Spring to learn a mortal's desires, the Mortal can't tell. The Changeling himself sees whatever special effects are thematic to him, but they're a personal hallucination. <br /> <br /> However, some Changeling magic has overtly supernatural effects, and those effects aren't hidden by the Mask. An Ogre Gargantuan who uses his Kith blessing will appear, in the eyes of humans around him, to be transformed into an 8-foot tall human, though his Mien will not otherwise show itself. <br /> <br /> It might make for a fun houserule to have mortals Ensorcelled by a Lost share in his contract hallucinations, but that'd be Houserule Territory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T19:28:18-07:00","id":219747,"title":"","content":"Worth mentioning: Mantle contributes some degree of SFX to Contract use - it's one of the marginally flashier aspects of Winter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T20:15:07-07:00","id":219788,"title":"","content":"True, but Mantle effects are tied into the Mien, and thus hidden by the Mask just like the horns and tusks and pointy ears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}